  "requestTimestamp": "2026-07-19T01:33:30.572Z",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nThe net taxable estate is ₱6,000,000 (₱12,000,000 gross estate - ₱6,000,000 allowable deductions). The estate tax is computed based on the net taxable estate using the graduated rates provided in the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Controlling Authorities\nThe computation of the net taxable estate and allowable deductions is governed by Section 34 of the NIRC, which outlines the deductions applicable to the estate tax.\n\n### Interpretation\nAccording to Section 34 of the NIRC, the allowable deductions from the gross estate include debts, funeral expenses, and other expenses that are necessary for the settlement of the estate. In this case, the gross estate is ₱12,000,000, and the allowable deductions amount to ₱6,000,000, resulting in a net taxable estate of ₱6,000,000.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nThe estate tax will be calculated based on the net taxable estate of ₱6,000,000. The estate tax rates are graduated, meaning that different portions of the estate will be taxed at different rates. It is essential to refer to the latest tax tables to determine the exact amount of estate tax due on the net taxable estate.",
